Indeed.  However, we can save the previous statement by construing
"a selbri must have a sumti of type P" as "a selbri which, when
applied to sumti not of type P, invariably produces falsehood".

Thus the x1 of "fetsi" "must be animate", meaning that when
it is inanimate, the resulting bridi is invariably false.

